  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only 2 of the 5 settings were confirmed, and only one of those clearly shows a weakness in the policy. Scene 023b7fcc with the cars 1 s later and 1.5x faster (S2) failed every time it was repeated. In each failure the ego's front hit car 56 in the left lane: in some runs the policy steered left out of its lane on its own, and in the others car 56 cut right in front of it. Scene 19f339ba with the cars 2 s later and 1.5x faster (S23) also failed every time, but the video review blames none of those failures on the policy. The lead car's replayed track jumps onto the ego, or a car behind drives into it at its recorded speed. S23 should be read as a fault in the traffic replay, not a challenging case. None of the other seven scenes failed at any setting tried, and the few settings repeated there kept the failure rate below one half.",
